1
00:00:08,030 --> 00:00:11,843
اَلْحَمْدُ لله ، وَالصَّلَاةُ وَالسَّلَامُ عَلى سَيِّدِنَا محمد وَعَلَى اَلِهِ وَصَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ

2
00:00:13,176 --> 00:00:17,777
Musa(موسى) was very shy and that is, how the mu'min(مؤمن); the believer should be.

3
00:00:18,404 --> 00:00:20,458
He was always covering up his body.

4
00:00:21,284 --> 00:00:29,415
Bani Israel(بني أسرائيل) said; Musa(موسى) is not showing us his body because, he's suffering from some kind of disease.

5
00:00:29,849 --> 00:00:37,374
And they accused him of leprosy, and they accused him of; they said that, syphilis; the expansion of the testicles.

6
00:00:38,194 --> 00:00:40,626
They said; That's why, he's always covering himself up.

7
00:00:40,993 --> 00:00:43,020
Bani Israel(بني أسرائيل); they used to bath together.

8
00:00:43,093 --> 00:00:48,610
They would go out in a river or in a pool, and they would all take their clothes, and they would just go in, and bath in front of each other.

9
00:00:48,963 --> 00:00:53,155
Musa(موسى) would go alone, and would bath alone, and would not let anyone see him.

10
00:00:54,589 --> 00:00:58,009
So, Allahسُبحانه وتعالى wanted Bani Israel(بني أسرائيل) to see that, this is not true.

11
00:00:58,922 --> 00:01:01,238
So, Musa(موسى) went to bath.

12
00:01:02,098 --> 00:01:05,280
So, he put his clothes on a rock; on a stone.

13
00:01:06,180 --> 00:01:10,377
And then when he look back; he didn't find the stone, the stone was running away with his clothes.

14
00:01:11,084 --> 00:01:15,571
So, Musa(موسى) is running after the stone, and this in Bukhari(بخاريْ); we'll read the Hadith.

15
00:01:15,864 --> 00:01:18,693
So Musa(موسى) is running after the stone, and he's saying;

16
00:01:18,733 --> 00:01:20,493
ثوبي يا حجر، ثوبي يا حجر

17
00:01:20,526 --> 00:01:23,207
Bring me my clothes back, stone! Bring me my clothes back!

18
00:01:23,514 --> 00:01:25,000
And he's running after the stone.

19
00:01:25,520 --> 00:01:32,702
And the stone took him around Bani Israel(بني أسرائيل) so, they could take a look at Musa(موسى); without any clothes.

20
00:01:34,242 --> 00:01:36,110
فَرَأَوْهُ أَحْسَنَ ما خَلَقَ اللَّهُ

21
00:01:36,130 --> 00:01:38,017
They saw the best creation of Allah.

22
00:01:38,937 --> 00:01:45,420
And then, when the issue was done, the stone stopped, by the order of Allah.

23
00:01:46,267 --> 00:01:52,366
So Musa(موسى) had a stick which he would carry with him always, and he started beating the rock; beating the stone.

24
00:01:52,886 --> 00:01:56,869
Rasool Allah ﷺ says; And he left on it marks, that could be seen.

25
00:01:57,289 --> 00:01:59,835
He hit it so hard that it left behind marks.

26
00:02:00,709 --> 00:02:07,191
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says; Oh you, who Believe! Be not; like those who annoyed Musa(موسى),

27
00:02:07,591 --> 00:02:13,908
but Allah cleared him of that which they alleged, and he was honorable before Allah.

28
00:02:14,728 --> 00:02:20,786
Syedina Musaعليه السلام was with the children of Israel(اسرائيل) in the wilderness.

29
00:02:21,553 --> 00:02:23,938
They got lost in the desert.

30
00:02:25,998 --> 00:02:36,832
And Syedina Musaعليه السلام had to spend his life and his efforts dealing with his people.

31
00:02:37,672 --> 00:02:39,462
And Musa(موسى) wanted good for them.

32
00:02:39,515 --> 00:02:44,418
Nevertheless, they were causing him difficulties, and they were being stubborn and difficult to deal with.

33
00:02:45,485 --> 00:02:47,685
So Musaعليه السلام told his people;

34
00:02:48,072 --> 00:02:51,978
وَإِذْ قَالَ مُوسَىٰ لِقَوْمِهِۦ يَٰقَوْمِ لِمَ تُؤْذُونَنِى وَقَد تَّعْلَمُونَ أَنِّى رَسُولُ ٱللَّهِ إِلَيْكُمْ ۖ

35
00:02:52,891 --> 00:02:55,021
Oh my people! Why do you harm me?

36
00:02:55,414 --> 00:02:58,408
When you know that, I am a messenger sent by Allah to you;

37
00:02:58,794 --> 00:02:59,848
why do you harm me?

38
00:03:00,714 --> 00:03:05,781
But Musa(موسى) had to endure all of this difficulty with his people.

39
00:03:07,954 --> 00:03:22,591
And then, his brother; Haroon عليه السلام; the prophet of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى; the right hand of Musa(موسى); his advisor; wazeer(وزير); his supporter; his helper throughout this period;

40
00:03:23,371 --> 00:03:25,931
His brother Haroon عليه السلام passed away.

41
00:03:28,031 --> 00:03:32,247
Now, Musaعليه السلام is alone to deal with his nation.

42
00:03:33,074 --> 00:03:36,667
With this huge nation of Bani Israel(بني أسرائيل); Musa(موسى) was alone.

43
00:03:36,993 --> 00:03:42,347
He lost his close associates, and brother, and advisor; Haroon عليه السلام.

44
00:03:43,867 --> 00:03:52,599
And then Musa(موسى) received a visit from the Angel of Death in the form of a man,

45
00:03:54,765 --> 00:03:56,417
and this Hadith(حديث) is in Bukhari(بخاريْ).

46
00:03:57,737 --> 00:04:05,243
The Angel of Death presented himself to Syedina Musa(سيدنا موسى); in the form of a human being; a man.

47
00:04:05,536 --> 00:04:09,603
And he came, and he told Musaعليه السلام; Are you ready to die?

48
00:04:10,436 --> 00:04:15,891
Because we know that, the Angel of Death takes our lives without announcement.

49
00:04:16,751 --> 00:04:21,222
But he does not take the life of a Nabi(نَبِي) until, they take permission, and they let them know.

50
00:04:23,188 --> 00:04:26,128
The Angel of Death told Musa(موسى); Are you ready to die?

51
00:04:28,175 --> 00:04:34,493
Musaعليه السلام slapped the angel of death in his face, and he knocked his eye out.

52
00:04:35,120 --> 00:04:38,738
He slapped him in his face, and he knocked his eye out.

53
00:04:40,265 --> 00:04:42,705
So, the Angel of Death went to Allahسُبحانه وتعالى and said;

54
00:04:42,725 --> 00:04:44,711
يا ربِّ أرسَلْتَني إلى عبدٍ لا يُريدُ الموتَ

55
00:04:44,778 --> 00:04:47,111
Oh Allah! You have sent me to a man who doesn't wanna die.

56
00:04:47,731 --> 00:04:52,963
And then the Angel of Death says in another Hadith(حديث); this is not in Bukhari(بخاريْ), I think this Hadith(حديث) was narrated by Imam Ahmad(اِمَامْ اَحْمَدْ).

57
00:04:53,249 --> 00:04:53,896
He says;

58
00:04:54,116 --> 00:04:58,029
ولولا كرامتُه عليك لشققتُ عليه

59
00:04:58,336 --> 00:05:04,409
And if it is not because, I know that Musa(موسى) is love to you, I would have made his death difficult.

60
00:05:04,936 --> 00:05:07,805
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى told the Angel of Death; Go back to Musa(موسی)

61
00:05:08,798 --> 00:05:12,258
and tell him to put his hand on the back of an ox

62
00:05:13,278 --> 00:05:20,035
and tell him that, every hair that is under his hand; I will give him one year in his life; for every hair under his hand.

63
00:05:20,781 --> 00:05:26,390
The Angel of Death went to Musa(موسى) and said; Oh Musa(موسى)! Allah is telling you put your hand on the back of an ox,

64
00:05:27,037 --> 00:05:30,830
and Allah will give you for every hair under your hand; one year to live.

65
00:05:31,737 --> 00:05:35,492
Musa(موسى) by now had chance to think about it.

66
00:05:37,139 --> 00:05:40,532
So, he asked the Angel of Death and then what, and then What will happen?

67
00:05:41,952 --> 00:05:43,966
Then the Angel of Death said; Then you will die.

68
00:05:44,386 --> 00:05:44,986
Musa(موسى) said;

69
00:05:45,006 --> 00:05:45,759
فالآنَ اَذِن

70
00:05:45,779 --> 00:05:46,788
Then let me die now.

71
00:05:47,342 --> 00:05:50,228
If in the end; I'm gonna die; let me die now.

72
00:05:50,895 --> 00:05:55,816
We don't know exactly, why Musa(موسى) rejected the angel of death in the beginning?

73
00:05:56,629 --> 00:05:58,049
But Ibn Kathir(اِبْنِ كَثِيْر) says;

74
00:05:58,243 --> 00:06:05,242
Maybe it was because Musa(موسى) had a desire in his heart that wasn't fulfilled yet.

75
00:06:06,235 --> 00:06:10,911
And Musa(موسى) wanted that desire; wanted that hope and aspiration to be fulfilled.

76
00:06:12,010 --> 00:06:21,280
And that desire, is a desire that Musa(موسى) has been living for, and awaiting for a long time in his life.

77
00:06:21,773 --> 00:06:25,573
And that is the promise of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى to enter into the Holy Land; Jerusalem.

78
00:06:28,013 --> 00:06:35,934
So Musa(موسى) wanted to have the honour of leading his people into the Holy Land and establishing the Islamic nation.

79
00:06:37,747 --> 00:06:41,060
He wanted to have the honour of leading his people into Jerusalem.

80
00:06:41,900 --> 00:06:48,290
But this was the will of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى and when Musa(موسى) realized that it wasn't ordained for him.

81
00:06:48,516 --> 00:06:49,796
He said; Then, let me die.

82
00:06:50,483 --> 00:06:51,885
But he said; I have a request.

83
00:06:52,931 --> 00:06:55,738
He told the Angel of death; I have one request.

84
00:06:56,698 --> 00:07:01,217
And that is, that you take me as close as you can, to Jerusalem;

85
00:07:02,064 --> 00:07:07,669
take me as close as you can, distance of throwing a stone, and let me die over there.

86
00:07:08,423 --> 00:07:15,815
If I'm not able to enter into Jerusalem alive, at least take me as close as possible to Jerusalem so that, I can die next to it.

87
00:07:16,221 --> 00:07:18,201
I can die next to the walls of Jerusalem.

88
00:07:18,855 --> 00:07:25,687
So Musaعليه السلام was living with the hope that one day, he will enter into the Holy Land.

89
00:07:26,460 --> 00:07:30,172
And the only reason; why he didn't, is because of who?

90
00:07:30,439 --> 00:07:31,399
Bani Israel(بني أسرائيل).

91
00:07:32,299 --> 00:07:35,966
They were on the Gates of Jerusalem, they were on the gates.

92
00:07:36,472 --> 00:07:38,372
Musa(موسى) told them; Let's go and fight.

93
00:07:38,586 --> 00:07:38,912
They said;

94
00:07:38,932 --> 00:07:41,506
فَاذْهَبْ أَنتَ وَرَبُّكَ فَقَاتِلَا إِنَّا هَاهُنَا قَاعِدُونَ۝

95
00:07:41,712 --> 00:07:44,281
Go and fight with your Lord, we're gonna stay right here.

96
00:07:44,754 --> 00:07:45,734
Then two men;

97
00:07:45,988 --> 00:07:47,308
أَنْعَمَ ٱللَّهُ عَلَيْهِمَا

98
00:07:47,488 --> 00:07:51,639
Two men; who fear Allahسُبحانه وتعالى whom, Allah has bestowed his blessing;

99
00:07:51,932 --> 00:07:53,614
they came to Bani Israel(بني أسرائيل) and they told them;

100
00:07:53,634 --> 00:07:56,664
اُدْخُلُوا عَلَيْهِمُ الْبَابَ فَإِذَا دَخَلْتُمُوهُ فَإِنَّكُمْ غَالِبُونَ ۚ

101
00:07:56,881 --> 00:08:01,914
Just walk through the gates and if you do so, you will win, and they refused.

102
00:08:02,734 --> 00:08:11,127
So Allahسُبحانه وتعالى did not give Bani Israel(بني أسرائيل), the honour of entering into Jerusalem because they don't deserve it; they're not ready yet.

103
00:08:11,614 --> 00:08:16,293
And because of that, Musa(موسى) was not able to enter into Jerusalem neither was his brother Haroon(هارون).

104
00:08:16,400 --> 00:08:20,367
And Musaعليه السلام died in Al-Tih(تیح); died in the wilderness.

105
00:08:22,067 --> 00:08:23,543
Rasool Allah ﷺ says;

106
00:08:23,705 --> 00:08:28,772
فلمَّا جاءَهُ صَكَّهُ ففقأَ فرجعَ إلى ربِّهِ فقالَ أرسَلتني إلى عبدٍ لا يريدُ الموتَ

107
00:08:29,384 --> 00:08:34,807
فردَّ اللَّهُ إليْهِ عينَهُ قالَ ارجِع فقل لَهُ يضعُ يدَهُ على متنِ ثورٍ

108
00:08:35,180 --> 00:08:39,434
فلَهُ بِكلِّ ما غطَّت يدُهُ بِكلِّ شعرةٍ سنةٌ

109
00:08:39,787 --> 00:08:42,607
قالَ أي ربِّ ثمَّ مَه قالَ الموتُ

110
00:08:42,867 --> 00:08:49,969
قالَ فالآنَ فسألَ اللَّهَ أن يدنيَهُ منَ الأرضِ المقدَّسةِ رميةً بحجرٍ

111
00:08:50,423 --> 00:08:56,010
قالَ رسولُ اللَّهِ صلَّى اللَّهُ عليْهِ وسلَّمَ فلو كنتُ ثَمَّ لأريتُكم قبرَهُ إلى جانبِ الطَّريقِ تحتَ الْكثيبِ الأحمرِ

112
00:08:56,190 --> 00:08:58,630
Rasool Allah ﷺ has seen the grave of Musa(موسى)

113
00:08:59,130 --> 00:09:02,219
and Rasool Ullah says, in the Hadith(حديث) of Al-Isra(اَلْاِسْرى);

114
00:09:02,365 --> 00:09:05,895
مررتُ بموسَى فاذا هو قائمٌ يُصلِّي في قبرِه

115
00:09:06,409 --> 00:09:10,955
Rasool Allah ﷺ says that; Indeed, in Al-Isra(اَلْاِسْرى), when Rasool Allah ﷺ travelled to Jerusalem;

116
00:09:11,095 --> 00:09:18,512
he passed next to the grave of Syedina Musa(سيدنا موسى), and he saw him praying in his grave to Allahسُبحانه وتعالى.

117
00:09:19,707 --> 00:09:29,390
We'll move on to a story; an interesting story; an amazing story, that occurred with Syedina Musa(سيدنا موسى).

118
00:09:29,950 --> 00:09:40,432
And the reason why I delayed it until now, is because we don't know exactly where the story fits, in terms of the chronological order of events.

119
00:09:41,238 --> 00:09:44,018
And this is the story of Musa(موسى) and Al-Khadr(الخضر).

120
00:09:44,638 --> 00:09:50,001
It is a story of Ajaa'ib(عجائب) of astonishing events from the beginning till the end.

121
00:09:50,627 --> 00:10:07,083
And the way this event happened, is that, Musa(موسى) stood one day on the minbar(منبر); on the pulpit, and was speaking to Bani Israel(بني أسرائيل).

122
00:10:08,837 --> 00:10:14,555
So, one of the men of Bani Israel(بني أسرائيل); the children of Israel(اسرائيل) stood up and said;

123
00:10:14,608 --> 00:10:19,573
Oh Musa(موسى)! Who is the most knowledgeable man, who's the most knowledgeable person?

124
00:10:20,800 --> 00:10:22,253
So Musa(موسى) said; I am.

125
00:10:23,040 --> 00:10:29,425
Because, he was the Prophet of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى; he was the Nabi(نَبِي); he is the one who's receiving revelation from Allahسُبحانه وتعالى.

126
00:10:29,779 --> 00:10:32,651
According to his knowledge, he is the most knowledgeable person.

127
00:10:33,391 --> 00:10:40,253
Because he is the Nabi(نَبِي); he is the Prophet; he is the one who has a direct link between him and Allah; receiving the Wahi(وحى) from Allahسُبحانه وتعالى.

128
00:10:41,046 --> 00:10:42,266
So he said; I am.

129
00:10:43,879 --> 00:10:45,884
And this Hadith(حديث) again in Bukhari(بخاريْ).

130
00:10:46,338 --> 00:10:50,820
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى told Musa(موسى); How come you did not say; Allah-u-Aalam(اللَّهُ أَعْلمَ)?

131
00:10:51,074 --> 00:10:55,800
How come you did not say that, Allah knows best, who's the most knowledgeable person?

132
00:10:56,360 --> 00:10:59,166
There is a man, who has knowledge that you do not have.

133
00:11:00,266 --> 00:11:05,154
Musa(موسى) did not say that, I am the most knowledgeable because he is proud or because he's arrogant.

134
00:11:05,267 --> 00:11:08,361
That's not the reason; Musa(موسى) is a Nabi(نَبِي) of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى; he would not do that.

135
00:11:08,974 --> 00:11:13,395
But he said that, he is the most knowledgeable person because that is according to his knowledge.

136
00:11:14,595 --> 00:11:19,341
So when it came to the knowledge of Musa(موسى) that, he is not the most knowledgeable person.

137
00:11:19,854 --> 00:11:26,280
He was so humble that he requested from Allahسُبحانه وتعالى to allow him to be a student of that man.

138
00:11:27,600 --> 00:11:29,787
He said; Oh Allah! How can I learn from him?

139
00:11:30,733 --> 00:11:37,089
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى told him; You can meet him in the place, where you miss or you lose your fish.

140
00:11:38,836 --> 00:11:49,758
That is where, you will meet this learned man. this wise man, and the name of this man is Al-Khadr(الخضر).

141
00:11:51,191 --> 00:11:55,765
And Rasool Allah ﷺ says in a Hadith(حديث); an authentic Hadith(حديث) that the reason, why he was called the Al-Khadr(الخضر)?

142
00:11:55,885 --> 00:11:57,857
Because Al-Khadr(الخضر); an Arabic means; green.

143
00:11:58,310 --> 00:12:00,270
The reason, why he was named Al-Khadr(الخضر)?

144
00:12:00,444 --> 00:12:07,399
Is because he was one sitting on dry grass, and when he stood up; the grass under him was green.

145
00:12:08,299 --> 00:12:10,353
So that is why, he was given the name Al-Khadr(الخضر);

146
00:12:10,959 --> 00:12:14,789
A karamah(الكرامۃ); some Karamat(کرامات) were happening on the hands of Al-Khadr(الخضر).

147
00:12:15,761 --> 00:12:19,995
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى told Musa(موسى) that you would meet Al-Khadr(الخضر) in this specific place.

148
00:12:21,042 --> 00:12:25,627
So Musa(موسى) took with him his servant, and who was the servant of  Musa(موسى)?

149
00:12:26,060 --> 00:12:27,517
Yusha Bin Noon(يوشع بن نون).

150
00:12:28,190 --> 00:12:30,984
Yusha Bin Noon(يوشع بن نون), and we're gonna talk about Yusha Bin Noon(يوشع بن نون) later.

151
00:12:31,197 --> 00:12:33,572
Yusha Bin Noon(يوشع بن نون) was the servant of Musa(موسى).

152
00:12:33,779 --> 00:12:37,698
And because he was close to Musa(موسى) and learning from Musa(موسى)

153
00:12:37,985 --> 00:12:43,004
then, Allahسُبحانه وتعالى appointed him to be the Nabi(نَبِي) of Bani Israel(بني أسرائيل) when Musa(موسى) passed away.

154
00:12:44,071 --> 00:12:46,084
Because he was close to Musa(موسى) and he was learning from Musa(موسى).

155
00:12:46,104 --> 00:12:49,904
That's how we learn by being close to the learned ones.

156
00:12:50,332 --> 00:12:55,166
So this servant of Musa(موسى) learn the wisdom and the knowledge from Musa(موسى),

157
00:12:55,293 --> 00:12:59,859
and then Allahسُبحانه وتعالى appointed him to be the Nabi(نَبِي) after Musa(موسى) and Haroon(هارون) passed away.

158
00:13:01,019 --> 00:13:04,284
So Musa(موسى) went with his servant and it's mentioned in Qur'an;

159
00:13:04,364 --> 00:13:05,551
وَإِذْ قَالَ لِفَتَاهُ

160
00:13:05,917 --> 00:13:13,676
He and his servant; they started embarking on this amazing and wonderful trip.

161
00:13:14,363 --> 00:13:15,669
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says;

162
00:13:15,936 --> 00:13:39,225
وَإِذْ قَالَ مُوسَىٰ لِفَتَاهُ لَا أَبْرَحُ حَتَّىٰ أَبْلُغَ مَجْمَعَ الْبَحْرَيْنِ أَوْ أَمْضِيَ حُقُبًا۝

163
00:13:39,992 --> 00:13:43,304
And remember when Musa(موسى) said to his boy servant;

164
00:13:43,684 --> 00:13:51,690
I will not give up travelling until I reach the junction of the two seas, or until I spend years and years in traveling.

165
00:13:51,943 --> 00:13:54,730
So, the place you will meet him is the junction between the two seas.

166
00:13:54,970 --> 00:13:59,380
Some of the scholars say that, these two seas are the Red Sea and the Mediterranean Sea.

167
00:14:00,393 --> 00:14:04,585
So you'll meet him in the junction between these two seas; Allah-u-Aalam(اللَّهُ أَعْلمَ).

168
00:14:05,272 --> 00:14:08,899
Musa(موسى) was so determined to go and learn.

169
00:14:09,205 --> 00:14:18,465
He said; I would reach to the junction of the seas even if it would take me years in travelling.

170
00:14:19,067 --> 00:14:22,420
Allahu Akbar(الله اكبر)! Musa(موسى) has so much knowledge already.

171
00:14:23,174 --> 00:14:25,517
He's already receiving the Wahi(وحى) from Allah.

172
00:14:26,350 --> 00:14:30,599
But because he knew that there is a man has some other knowledge that he does not have.

173
00:14:30,859 --> 00:14:34,405
He's willing to make all of this travelling to go and learn.

174
00:14:34,838 --> 00:14:36,558
This is how Talib-al'ilm(طالب العلم) should be!

175
00:14:36,825 --> 00:14:39,278
The students of knowledge needs to sacrifice.

176
00:14:39,678 --> 00:14:41,797
You need to sacrifice to learn.

177
00:14:42,117 --> 00:14:44,624
Musa(موسى); even though, he was knowledgeable.

178
00:14:44,797 --> 00:14:53,315
He did not say, what I have is enough, he travelled all the way, and he said, I would even travel years, if I need to do so, to go and learn.

179
00:14:53,755 --> 00:14:55,857
So we need to sacrifice if we want to learn.

180
00:14:55,990 --> 00:14:59,303
We need to sacrifice time and effort and money to learn.

181
00:15:00,130 --> 00:15:02,875
The servant of Musa(موسى) was carrying this fish.

182
00:15:03,868 --> 00:15:05,221
It was a dead fish.

183
00:15:06,168 --> 00:15:09,207
They camped in a certain area and they went to sleep.

184
00:15:09,900 --> 00:15:14,887
But something amazing happened, and this is the starting of the amazing things in this trip.

185
00:15:15,640 --> 00:15:26,655
This fish woke up and marched all the way to the sea, and started swimming in the sea in front of the eyes of Yusha Bin Noon(يوشع بن نون).

186
00:15:27,541 --> 00:15:33,028
Yusha Bin Noon(يوشع بن نون) saw this dead fish wake up, and then march all the way to the sea,

187
00:15:33,161 --> 00:15:36,033
and then start swimming in the sea, and it's making a tunnel behind it.

188
00:15:36,113 --> 00:15:36,790
السربة

189
00:15:37,367 --> 00:15:41,388
He forgot to tell us about it, and they went to bed and then they travel.

190
00:15:42,381 --> 00:15:43,554
They travelled the next day.

191
00:15:43,641 --> 00:15:44,974
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says;

192
00:15:45,234 --> 00:15:47,517
فَلَمَّا بَلَغَا مَجْمَعَ بَيْنِهِمَا

193
00:15:48,011 --> 00:15:50,537
Then they reach to the junction of the two seas.

194
00:15:51,371 --> 00:15:54,506
Musa(موسى) now was tired and hungry.

195
00:15:55,000 --> 00:15:59,173
And Rasool Allah ﷺ says; Musa(موسى) did not become tired and hungry until that moment;

196
00:15:59,573 --> 00:16:06,942
All throughout this trip until that moment, Musa(موسى) never felt exhausted and then Musa(موسى) said;

197
00:16:07,169 --> 00:16:32,609
فَلَمَّا جَاوَزَا قَالَ لِفَتَىٰهُ ءَاتِنَا غَدَآءَنَا لَقَدْ لَقِينَا مِن سَفَرِنَا هَٰذَا نَصَبًا۝

198
00:16:33,355 --> 00:16:38,046
So, they reached to the junction of the two seas; they slept there and then, they travelled the next day.

199
00:16:38,146 --> 00:16:43,225
So when they had passed further on, beyond the fixed place,

200
00:16:43,412 --> 00:16:50,343
Musa(موسى) said to his boy servant; Bring us our morning meal, truly we have suffered much fatigue in this journey.

201
00:16:51,130 --> 00:16:56,495
Only then, did Musa(موسى) feel fatigue, and he told his servants bring us the fish.

202
00:16:57,109 --> 00:16:59,469
Yusha Bin Noon(يوشع بن نون) remembered; what happened to the fish.

203
00:16:59,722 --> 00:17:00,415
He said;

204
00:17:00,755 --> 00:17:29,758
قَالَ أَرَأَيْتَ إِذْ أَوَيْنَا إِلَى الصَّخْرَةِ فَإِنِّي نَسِيتُ الْحُوتَ وَمَا أَنسَانِيهُ إِلَّا الشَّيْطَانُ أَنْ أَذْكُرَهُ ۚ

205
00:17:30,511 --> 00:17:35,250
He said; Do you remember when we betook ourselves to the rock; that's where they slept; next to the rock.

206
00:17:35,970 --> 00:17:42,587
I indeed forgot the fish, none but Shaytan(شَيْطَانْ) made me forget to remember it.

207
00:17:42,934 --> 00:17:46,280
It took its course into the sea in a strange way.

208
00:17:47,266 --> 00:17:49,793
Musa(موسى) said; That is what we were looking for.

209
00:17:50,813 --> 00:17:55,545
Because Allahسُبحانه وتعالى told Musa(موسى) you will find Al-Khadr(الخضر) in the place where you lose the fish.

210
00:17:56,538 --> 00:17:57,118
So Musa(موسى) said;

211
00:17:57,138 --> 00:17:58,208
ذَٰلِكَ مَا كُنَّا نَبْغِ ۚ

212
00:17:58,248 --> 00:18:00,968
That's what I was waiting for.

213
00:18:01,622 --> 00:18:05,447
قَالَ ذَٰلِكَ مَا كُنَّا نَبْغِ ۚ فَٱرْتَدَّا عَلَىٰٓ ءَاثَارِهِمَا قَصَصًا۝

214
00:18:05,467 --> 00:18:08,712
Musa(موسى) said; That is what we have been seeking.

215
00:18:09,165 --> 00:18:11,738
So they went back retracing their footsteps.

216
00:18:11,958 --> 00:18:17,051
Now, Musa(موسى) and Yusha Bin Noon(يوشع بن نون); they have to travel back the same way.

217
00:18:17,191 --> 00:18:21,396
Because, Allah told Musa(موسى) you would find him in the place where you lose the fish.

218
00:18:21,629 --> 00:18:25,496
Already, they've travelled a long distance. Now, they have to retract back.

219
00:18:25,709 --> 00:18:29,917
So, Musa(موسى) and Yusha Bin Noon(يوشع بن نون) are retracing their steps back.

220
00:18:30,524 --> 00:18:36,094
On their way back; they passed by a man who was covered under his blanket.

221
00:18:36,554 --> 00:18:39,880
So Musa(موسى) saw that man, and he told them; Assalam-o-Alaykum(اسلام عليكم)!

222
00:18:40,160 --> 00:18:41,427
So the man stood up and said;

223
00:18:41,460 --> 00:18:42,780
أَنَّى بأرضِكَ السَّلامُ

224
00:18:43,280 --> 00:18:47,092
He said; People over here do not know about Salam(سلام).

225
00:18:48,599 --> 00:18:49,465
Who are you?

226
00:18:50,279 --> 00:18:52,968
Musa(موسى) said; I am Musa(موسى)!

227
00:18:53,808 --> 00:18:56,148
So the man said; Musa(موسى); Bani Israel(بني أسرائيل).

228
00:18:56,341 --> 00:18:59,181
Are you the Musa(موسى) of the children of Israel(اسرائيل)?

229
00:18:59,521 --> 00:19:00,480
Musa(موسى) said; Yes!

230
00:19:01,066 --> 00:19:03,533
 Al-Khadr(الخضر) already knew him and heard about him.

231
00:19:04,240 --> 00:19:07,100
So when he said; I am Musa(موسى), he said; Are you the Musa(موسى) of Bani Israel(بني أسرائيل)?

232
00:19:07,173 --> 00:19:09,075
He wants to make sure. He said; Yes!

233
00:19:09,329 --> 00:19:10,895
I'm Musa(موسى); Bani Israel(بني أسرائيل).

234
00:19:12,035 --> 00:19:13,037
He said; I am Al-Khadr(الخضر)!

235
00:19:13,711 --> 00:19:15,710
Musaعليه السلام told Al-Khadr(الخضر);

236
00:19:16,016 --> 00:19:22,349
I want to learn from you; humble; a Nabi(نَبِي) of Allah; he's telling this man, who might not be a Nabi(نَبِي).

237
00:19:23,149 --> 00:19:25,932
Because, there's a difference of opinion whether, Al-Khadr(الخضر) is a Nabi(نَبِي) or not.

238
00:19:26,295 --> 00:19:28,857
Some scholars say; he is, some say; he's not.

239
00:19:29,304 --> 00:19:34,624
And it is an undetermined issue because, there is no evidence that he was a Nabi(نَبِي) of Allah.

240
00:19:34,930 --> 00:19:39,370
He could have been of the Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء) or he could have been a Wali(ولي) of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى.

241
00:19:39,484 --> 00:19:40,413
So, we don't know.

242
00:19:40,693 --> 00:19:48,719
Regardless, it shows that Musa(موسى) wanted to learn from him, and he came in a very humble manner, and he said; I want to study; under you.

243
00:19:48,966 --> 00:19:55,064
Al-Khadr(الخضر) said; I have knowledge, that Allah has taught me, that you do not have;

244
00:19:55,831 --> 00:19:59,885
and you have knowledge, which Allah taught you that, I do not have.

245
00:20:00,985 --> 00:20:07,713
So, Al-Khadr(الخضر); he knew, that he has some knowledge that is unknown to Musa(موسى),

246
00:20:07,847 --> 00:20:10,687
and Musa(موسى) has some knowledge, that is unknown to him.

247
00:20:11,867 --> 00:20:14,759
Musa(موسى) said; I want to follow you.

248
00:20:15,546 --> 00:20:16,132
أَتَّبِعُكَ

249
00:20:16,346 --> 00:20:17,752
I want to follow you.

250
00:20:18,412 --> 00:20:23,725
Al-Khadr(الخضر) said; You will not be able to follow me because you will have no patience.

251
00:20:24,098 --> 00:20:34,171
وَكَيْفَ تَصْبِرُ عَلَىٰ مَا لَمْ تُحِطْ بِهِۦ خُبْرًا۝

252
00:20:34,797 --> 00:20:38,024
How will you have patience on something that you did not know?

253
00:20:38,517 --> 00:20:42,979
You gonna see things that are amazing and astonishing and you're not gonna have patience.

254
00:20:44,144 --> 00:20:47,848
Musa(موسى) said; Let me follow you! Let me follow you!

255
00:20:48,448 --> 00:20:53,586
Al-Khadr(الخضر) did not want to reject this student of knowledge, but he set a condition,

256
00:20:54,479 --> 00:20:55,106
he said;

257
00:20:55,372 --> 00:21:17,406
قَالَ فَإِنِ اتَّبَعْتَنِي فَلَا تَسْأَلْنِي عَن شَيْءٍ حَتَّىٰ أُحْدِثَ لَكَ مِنْهُ ذِكْرًا۝

258
00:21:18,059 --> 00:21:25,518
He said; If you follow me, asked me not about anything, till I myself mentioned it to you.

259
00:21:26,298 --> 00:21:31,140
This is the condition, you follow me; but you do not question my actions.

260
00:21:31,874 --> 00:21:34,302
You accept what you see; don't argue.

261
00:21:34,822 --> 00:21:36,124
Musa(موسى) said; I agree.

262
00:21:36,724 --> 00:21:38,611
So this was their agreement.

263
00:21:40,424 --> 00:21:42,227
They began this trip.

264
00:21:42,547 --> 00:21:44,813
Al-Khadr(الخضر) is taking Musa(موسى) to Wonderland.

265
00:21:45,753 --> 00:21:51,332
It started with Al-Khadr(الخضر) and Musa(موسى) crossing the sea.

266
00:21:52,059 --> 00:21:56,139
Al-Khadr(الخضر) wanted to travel to the other side of the sea.

267
00:21:56,930 --> 00:22:00,664
So he was looking for transportation; for a ship.

268
00:22:01,797 --> 00:22:08,605
So he found the ship and he asked them to deliver them to the other side.

269
00:22:09,005 --> 00:22:17,197
It turned out that the sailors; the owners of the ship; knew Al-Khadr(الخضر), and they offered him a free ride.

270
00:22:18,124 --> 00:22:19,817
We're gonna carry you for free.

271
00:22:20,551 --> 00:22:25,028
They didn't do it; because they know Musa(موسى); they did it; because they know Al-Khadr(الخضر).

272
00:22:25,508 --> 00:22:29,475
So, this was a favour done to who? To Al-Khadr(الخضر); specifically.

273
00:22:29,828 --> 00:22:30,959
They knew Al-Khadr(الخضر).

274
00:22:31,773 --> 00:22:34,066
Rasool Allah ﷺ mentions that in the Hadith(حديث);

275
00:22:34,366 --> 00:22:35,653
فحملوهما بغير نَوْلٍ

276
00:22:35,713 --> 00:22:38,639
They carried them without any compensation; why?

277
00:22:38,686 --> 00:22:39,993
Because they knew Al-Khadr(الخضر).

278
00:22:41,459 --> 00:22:48,405
The first thing that happened when they were on this ship; Musa(موسى) and Al-Khadr(الخضر) was sitting together on the deck;

279
00:22:48,978 --> 00:22:58,106
and a bird landed on the deck; and then that bird dipped its beak in the ocean; in the sea to drink.

280
00:22:59,439 --> 00:23:01,898
Al-Khadr(الخضر) told Musa(موسى); Did you see that bird?

281
00:23:03,051 --> 00:23:04,125
Musa(موسى) said; Yes!

282
00:23:04,158 --> 00:23:12,930
Al-Khadr(الخضر) said; My knowledge plus your knowledge compared to the knowledge of Allah is like; what that bird has taken from the sea.

283
00:23:14,657 --> 00:23:19,642
That's one drop, that the bird has taken from the sea is like; my knowledge plus your knowledge.

284
00:23:19,942 --> 00:23:23,144
You said that, you're the most knowledgeable person on the face of the Earth.

285
00:23:23,404 --> 00:23:26,797
Allah told you that, there's somebody who has more knowledge than you;

286
00:23:26,970 --> 00:23:32,390
we together; me and you together combined the knowledge of the most two knowledgeable people on the Earth,

287
00:23:32,750 --> 00:23:36,676
compared to the knowledge of Allah is less than what, that bird has taken from the sea.

288
00:23:37,496 --> 00:23:41,109
That is the knowledge of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى; the ocean of the knowledge of Allah.

289
00:23:41,323 --> 00:23:43,476
That's the first lesson Al-Khadr(الخضر) is giving to Musa(موسى).

290
00:23:43,809 --> 00:23:46,395
Our knowledge is nothing compared to the knowledge of Allah.

291
00:23:47,955 --> 00:23:51,780
And then Al-Khadr(الخضر); When the sailors were busy with work,

292
00:23:52,134 --> 00:24:01,741
Al-Khadr(الخضر) took an axe, and he broke a slab on the ship, and he plucked out a panel.

293
00:24:02,181 --> 00:24:03,888
He destroyed part of the ship.

294
00:24:04,141 --> 00:24:09,227
He took his axe and he started destroying it when the sailors were busy; they didn't know what was happening.

295
00:24:09,360 --> 00:24:12,560
And then he pulled out the panel from the ship.

296
00:24:13,427 --> 00:24:16,201
Musa(موسى); when he saw this, he couldn't believe his eyes.

297
00:24:17,008 --> 00:24:19,855
Because these men are doing you a favour;

298
00:24:19,908 --> 00:24:23,887
they're doing it for you not for me; they're doing you a favour by giving you a ride for free

299
00:24:24,221 --> 00:24:26,227
and you destroyed their ship.

300
00:24:27,341 --> 00:24:28,754
Musaعليه السلام said;

301
00:24:29,327 --> 00:24:57,984
فَٱنطَلَقَا حَتَّىٰٓ إِذَا رَكِبَا فِى ٱلسَّفِينَةِ خَرَقَهَا ۖ قَالَ أَخَرَقْتَهَا لِتُغْرِقَ أَهْلَهَا لَقَدْ جِئْتَ شَيْـًٔا إِمْرًا۝

302
00:24:58,327 --> 00:25:03,387
So they then proceeded till when they embark the ship; Al-Khadr(الخضر) scuttled it.

303
00:25:03,880 --> 00:25:08,063
Musa(موسى) said; Have you scuttled it in order to drown his people;

304
00:25:08,196 --> 00:25:11,019
verily, you have committed that thing that is evil.

305
00:25:11,512 --> 00:25:12,506
How could you do this?

306
00:25:13,432 --> 00:25:15,971
How could you do this for the people who are doing you a favour?

307
00:25:16,198 --> 00:25:18,371
Is this; is this how you pay them back?

308
00:25:18,711 --> 00:25:21,264
They give you a ride for free and you destroy their ship.

309
00:25:21,637 --> 00:25:23,577
Do you want them to drown in the sea?

310
00:25:25,117 --> 00:25:28,165
Al-Khadr(الخضر) said; Didn't I tell you, you're not gonna have patience?

311
00:25:30,032 --> 00:25:32,572
The agreement was that, you don't question my actions.

312
00:25:33,678 --> 00:25:36,422
قَالَ أَلَمْ أَقُل لَّكَ إِنَّكَ لَن تَسْتَطِيعَ مَعِيَ صَبْرًا۝

313
00:25:36,649 --> 00:25:38,702
Didn't I tell you, you're not gonna have patience.

314
00:25:40,209 --> 00:25:44,691
Musa(موسى) did not intentionally break his promise; Musa(موسى) forgot.

315
00:25:45,197 --> 00:25:46,291
Rasool Allah ﷺ says;

316
00:25:46,331 --> 00:25:48,441
وَكانَتِ الأُولَى مِن مُوسَى نِسْيانًا

317
00:25:48,604 --> 00:25:50,224
The first time, Musa(موسى) forgot.

318
00:25:50,404 --> 00:25:53,224
Musa(موسى) forgot; forgot his promise.

319
00:25:55,417 --> 00:25:56,623
So he told Al-Khadr(الخضر);

320
00:25:57,030 --> 00:26:13,552
قَالَ لَا تُؤَاخِذْنِى بِمَا نَسِيتُ وَلَا تُرْهِقْنِى مِنْ أَمْرِى عُسْرًا۝

321
00:26:14,185 --> 00:26:23,085
Musa(موسى) said; Call me not to account for what I forgot, and be not hard upon me for my affair with you.

322
00:26:24,371 --> 00:26:28,888
Musa(موسى) said; Forgive me for this mistake, and don't be hard,

323
00:26:28,908 --> 00:26:36,394
meaning; I mean, even though our agreement is; if I question you, our agreement is breached.

324
00:26:36,734 --> 00:26:38,426
But he said; I mean, give me another chance.

325
00:26:38,733 --> 00:26:40,826
Don't be strict; give me another chance.

326
00:26:42,040 --> 00:26:44,036
Al-Khadr(الخضر) said; I'll give you another chance.

327
00:26:44,722 --> 00:26:48,431
Even though, the agreement is over with, Al-Khadr(الخضر) could have told Musa(موسى), you have to leave.

328
00:26:48,831 --> 00:26:50,631
But Al-Khadr(الخضر) said; I will give you another chance.

329
00:26:52,051 --> 00:26:54,324
They reached to the shore on the other side.

330
00:26:55,251 --> 00:26:59,626
And they passed by children who were playing.

331
00:27:01,326 --> 00:27:03,673
What seemed to be innocent children playing?

332
00:27:05,086 --> 00:27:07,434
Al-Khadr(الخضر) walked up to one of these children.

333
00:27:07,840 --> 00:27:11,987
He picked him up; he grabbed his head; and he tore it off.

334
00:27:13,000 --> 00:27:15,387
He tore off the head of the child; he killed him.

335
00:27:17,439 --> 00:27:21,324
Musaعليه السلام remembers exactly his promise.

336
00:27:21,731 --> 00:27:22,911
Now, he remembers it.

337
00:27:23,778 --> 00:27:27,201
But we know the nature of Syedina Musa(سيدنا موسى); he can never approve evil.

338
00:27:27,221 --> 00:27:31,218
If he sees something that is wrong; he speaks out against it.

339
00:27:31,980 --> 00:27:36,638
So Musaعليه السلام; even though, he knows that he has given a promise not to question;

340
00:27:36,878 --> 00:27:40,285
when he saw this crime in front of his eyes, he said;

341
00:27:40,978 --> 00:28:14,341
فَانطَلَقَا حَتَّىٰ إِذَا لَقِيَا غُلَامًا فَقَتَلَهُ قَالَ أَقَتَلْتَ نَفْسًا زَكِيَّةً بِغَيْرِ نَفْسٍ لَّقَدْ جِئْتَ شَيْئًا نُّكْرًا۝

342
00:28:15,014 --> 00:28:19,627
Have you killed an innocent person who killed none?

343
00:28:19,813 --> 00:28:22,400
Verily, you have committed that dreadful thing.

344
00:28:23,093 --> 00:28:24,122
How could you do this?

345
00:28:24,329 --> 00:28:25,522
This child is innocent.

346
00:28:25,815 --> 00:28:26,815
He didn't do anything.

347
00:28:27,062 --> 00:28:28,115
How come you killed them?

348
00:28:28,942 --> 00:28:29,782
Al-Khadr(الخضر) said;

349
00:28:30,175 --> 00:28:33,714
قَالَ أَلَمْ أَقُل لَّكَ إِنَّكَ لَن تَسْتَطِيعَ مَعِيَ صَبْرًا۝

350
00:28:33,834 --> 00:28:36,232
Didn't I tell you, you're not gonna have patience.

351
00:28:37,798 --> 00:28:43,977
So the anger of Musa(موسى) subceeded, and he told Al-Khadr(الخضر); This is my last chance.

352
00:28:44,577 --> 00:28:47,300
قَالَ إِن سَأَلْتُكَ عَن شَىْءٍ بَعْدَهَا فَلَا تُصَٰحِبْنِى ۖ

353
00:28:48,107 --> 00:28:49,989
He said; Give me one more chance.

354
00:28:50,415 --> 00:28:53,095
Three strikes or you're out; this is my last chance.

355
00:28:54,402 --> 00:28:55,829
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says;

356
00:28:56,176 --> 00:29:17,969
قَالَ إِن سَأَلْتُكَ عَن شَىْءٍ بَعْدَهَا فَلَا تُصَٰحِبْنِى ۖ قَدْ بَلَغْتَ مِن لَّدُنِّى عُذْرًا۝

357
00:29:18,162 --> 00:29:24,721
Musa(موسى) said; If I asked you anything after this, keep me not in your company, you have received the excuse from me.

358
00:29:24,741 --> 00:29:25,095
That's it.

359
00:29:25,175 --> 00:29:26,208
You have done your part.

360
00:29:26,595 --> 00:29:27,981
And you have forgive me enough.

361
00:29:28,221 --> 00:29:31,250
One more time; give me one more chance; the third chance.

362
00:29:31,684 --> 00:29:36,386
If I break the promise for a third time, then you can go your own way.

363
00:29:37,799 --> 00:29:39,012
Al-Khadr(الخضر) agreed.

364
00:29:40,179 --> 00:29:45,721
فَانطَلَقَا حَتَّىٰ إِذَا أَتَيَا أَهْلَ قَرْيَةٍ اسْتَطْعَمَا أَهْلَهَا فَأَبَوْا أَن يُضَيِّفُوهُمَا

365
00:29:46,394 --> 00:29:53,246
Musa(موسى) and Al-Khadr(الخضر) walked into a town, and they asked the people of that town to feed them.

366
00:29:54,520 --> 00:30:02,122
It was in their law; in their religion, and in our religion too, and that the guest has a right upon you.

367
00:30:02,516 --> 00:30:07,187
You are not doing the guests the favour by providing for the guests for three days.

368
00:30:07,561 --> 00:30:12,113
And it's an obligation on you to help the guest and take care of that guests for three days.

369
00:30:12,179 --> 00:30:17,079
After three days, you can hold back if you want, or you can continue, but its upto you.

370
00:30:17,391 --> 00:30:22,528
But for the first three days, it's an obligation on the Muslim community to take care of the guest.

371
00:30:24,121 --> 00:30:29,361
So, Musa(موسى) and Al-Khadr(الخضر); they walked into that town; they asked them to feed them; they provided them with nothing.

372
00:30:29,921 --> 00:30:35,280
They were very stingy people; they refuse to help; they did not extend any helping hand to them.

373
00:30:35,533 --> 00:30:40,212
While, Al-Khadr(الخضر) and Musa(موسى) were walking down the street in that town.

374
00:30:40,525 --> 00:30:46,571
Al-Khadr(الخضر) saw a wall that was about to fall down; cracked wall; very weak; it was about to tumble and fall down.

375
00:30:47,817 --> 00:30:52,063
Al-Khadr(الخضر) started erecting the wall again.

376
00:30:53,210 --> 00:30:59,549
Al-Khadr(الخضر) stopped, and he was rebuilding that wall without taking permission from anyone;

377
00:30:59,715 --> 00:31:06,789
without being requested to do so by anyone; and he's doing it for free; he's building that wall for free.

378
00:31:07,498 --> 00:31:09,358
Musa(موسى) saw contradiction in this.

379
00:31:10,191 --> 00:31:14,011
The people of the ship; the sailors of the ship who are doing you a favour for free.

380
00:31:14,564 --> 00:31:15,604
You destroyed their ship.

381
00:31:15,931 --> 00:31:18,704
The child who's innocent; you kill him.

382
00:31:19,311 --> 00:31:24,046
And these people who refuse to help us; you're doing them a favour for free.

383
00:31:24,820 --> 00:31:28,073
The people who will help you; you do what seems to be harming them.

384
00:31:28,326 --> 00:31:32,499
And the people who are not doing you any good; you are helping them.

385
00:31:32,906 --> 00:31:35,693
So, Musa(موسى) had the suggestion to offer. He said;

386
00:31:35,886 --> 00:31:37,906
قَالَ لَوْ شِئْتَ لَتَّخَذْتَ عَلَيْهِ أَجْرًا۝

387
00:31:38,053 --> 00:31:40,771
Why don't you charge them for building the wall?

388
00:31:41,464 --> 00:31:42,704
Why don't you charge them?

389
00:31:43,004 --> 00:31:43,724
Al-Khadr(الخضر) said;

390
00:31:43,837 --> 00:31:52,536
قَالَ هَٰذَا فِرَاقُ بَيْنِى وَبَيْنِكَ ۚ

391
00:31:53,130 --> 00:31:55,083
This is the end of our agreement.

392
00:31:55,790 --> 00:31:58,997
You have breached the agreement; you have to go your way, and I go my way.

393
00:31:59,143 --> 00:32:00,307
It's done.

394
00:32:01,433 --> 00:32:03,447
But Al-Khadr(الخضر) said; Before you leave;

395
00:32:03,767 --> 00:32:06,815
سَأُنَبِّئُكَ بِتَأْوِيلِ مَا لَمْ تَسْتَطِع عَّلَيْهِ صَبْرًا۝

396
00:32:06,849 --> 00:32:11,509
I will tell you the interpretation of the things, you did not have patience on.

397
00:32:12,229 --> 00:32:15,061
I will interpret for you what was happening.

398
00:32:15,654 --> 00:32:51,231
أَمَّا ٱلسَّفِينَةُ فَكَانَتْ لِمَسَٰكِينَ يَعْمَلُونَ فِى ٱلْبَحْرِ فَأَرَدتُّ أَنْ أَعِيبَهَا وَكَانَ وَرَآءَهُم مَّلِكٌ يَأْخُذذُ كُلَّ سَفِينَةٍ غَصْبًا۝

399
00:32:51,551 --> 00:32:53,378
He said; I'll tell you first about the ship.

400
00:32:54,084 --> 00:32:58,302
That ship belong to some poor sailors.

401
00:32:58,689 --> 00:33:00,962
That was their source of living.

402
00:33:01,702 --> 00:33:05,921
They would use that ship for transportation or for fishing.

403
00:33:06,155 --> 00:33:08,235
But that was their only source of income.

404
00:33:08,761 --> 00:33:13,414
And there was a king on the way, who was attacking the area.

405
00:33:14,067 --> 00:33:19,763
And that King is going to take every ship that seems to be in a good condition.

406
00:33:21,436 --> 00:33:31,074
So the king is gonna come in that area, and is gonna take by force, and confiscate every ship that seemed to be in a good condition.

407
00:33:31,474 --> 00:33:34,654
So, Al-Khadr(الخضر) wanted to break this ship.

408
00:33:35,274 --> 00:33:38,620
So that, it seems to be an old destroyed ship.

409
00:33:39,034 --> 00:33:40,674
So the king would leave it alone.

410
00:33:41,620 --> 00:33:48,917
And therefore, these poor sailors would not have lost their ship and then they can fix it after the king leaves.

411
00:33:49,977 --> 00:33:53,879
That is why, I broke off a panel from it.

412
00:33:54,966 --> 00:33:58,426
So at least the sailors will have their ship, even though, it's not functioning; they will have it.

413
00:33:58,959 --> 00:34:02,655
But if I did not do this, the king would take the whole thing away.

414
00:34:03,595 --> 00:34:05,588
And they would lose their source of income.

415
00:34:05,668 --> 00:34:13,124
So Allahسُبحانه وتعالى brought for these poor sailors a blessing through the hands of Al-Khadr(الخضر).

416
00:34:13,951 --> 00:34:23,913
And by the way, this Ayah(آية) has been used as a supporting evidence for the issue of; Al-Fiqh al-masa'il al-mafasid(الفقه المسائل المفاسد).

417
00:34:24,445 --> 00:34:27,831
And the scholars derived the rule from this Ayah(آية) that,

418
00:34:27,978 --> 00:34:35,987
if you are confronted with two evils, and you must choose between one of them; you choose the least,

419
00:34:37,240 --> 00:34:39,855
or like they say; necessary evil.

420
00:34:40,593 --> 00:34:43,966
If you have to choose between two evils; choose the least.

421
00:34:45,086 --> 00:34:46,220
There were two evils here;

422
00:34:46,260 --> 00:34:48,373
One evil was; the king takes away the ship.

423
00:34:48,753 --> 00:34:55,579
The other evil is; I break a panel, which is the least evil; breaking a panel, breaking that slab.

424
00:34:55,952 --> 00:35:00,724
Al-Khadr(الخضر) had this Fiqh(فقه) of choosing the least of the two evils.

425
00:35:01,424 --> 00:35:02,938
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says;

426
00:35:03,564 --> 00:35:07,303
As for the ship; it belonged to poor people working in the sea.

427
00:35:07,563 --> 00:35:14,302
So, I wish to make a defective damage in it, as there was a king behind them who seized every ship by force.

428
00:35:14,902 --> 00:35:16,916
Next the story of Al-Ghulam(الغلام);

429
00:35:17,489 --> 00:35:41,212
وَأَمَّا ٱلْغُلَٰمُ فَكَانَ أَبَوَاهُ مُؤْمِنَيْنِ فَخَشِينَآ أَن يُرْهِقَهُمَا طُغْيَٰنًا وَكُفْرًا۝

430
00:35:41,965 --> 00:35:50,934
He said; That young boy; he was going to grow up to be a Kafir(كافر); a disbeliever, and a tyrant.

431
00:35:51,747 --> 00:35:53,747
يُرْهِقَهُمَا طُغْيَٰنًا وَكُفْرًا۝

432
00:35:53,927 --> 00:35:57,413
Tughyan(طُغْيَٰن) is tyranny and Kuffr(كفر) is disbelief.

433
00:35:58,219 --> 00:36:07,620
So, this young boy will grow up not only to be a nonbeliever in Allah, but he will grow up to be a tyrant, and will cause his parents; hardship and difficulty.

434
00:36:08,166 --> 00:36:11,901
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى wanted the best for this family.

435
00:36:13,048 --> 00:36:17,559
So Allah wanted to take away the life of that young boy,

436
00:36:18,446 --> 00:36:26,997
and to replace the family with another child that will be nice and kind to his parents, and will be a believer in Allah.

437
00:36:27,677 --> 00:36:31,490
 And this shows you that you never know, what lies on the other side.

438
00:36:32,357 --> 00:36:37,093
These parents; let's think about their reaction when their child was killed; What do you think their reaction was?

439
00:36:37,593 --> 00:36:40,934
 They would cry, and they would mourn, and they would be upset and sorry.

440
00:36:41,574 --> 00:36:44,081
Because they do not know what Allah is planning for them.

441
00:36:44,561 --> 00:36:46,427
Al-Khadr(الخضر) knew the plan, but they didn't.

442
00:36:47,614 --> 00:36:52,812
They were losing a child, but they did not know that, that was the best for them.

443
00:36:52,965 --> 00:36:58,754
Because if this child grew up and was living, he would cause them; hardship and difficulty.

444
00:36:58,974 --> 00:37:05,732
And Allahسُبحانه وتعالى wanted to take away this child and to give them another child, that will grow up and become kind to them.

445
00:37:05,945 --> 00:37:11,144
So, Allahسُبحانه وتعالى was hiding for this family good in what appeared to be evil.

446
00:37:11,558 --> 00:37:15,311
You might love something, but it's not good for you.

447
00:37:16,064 --> 00:37:19,270
And you might dislike something, but it's good for you.

448
00:37:20,297 --> 00:37:28,439
Allah says; As for the boy, his parents were believers, and we feared lest he should oppress them by rebellion and disbelief.

449
00:37:28,812 --> 00:37:36,618
So we intended that their Lord should change him for them, for one better in righteousness and near to mercy.

450
00:37:37,678 --> 00:37:39,769
Next the story of the wall.

451
00:37:40,622 --> 00:37:42,542
Al-Khadr(الخضر) erected the wall.

452
00:37:43,502 --> 00:37:48,065
Al-Khadr(الخضر) said; That wall belonged to two orphans in the town.

453
00:37:50,365 --> 00:37:52,348
Beneath the wall was a treasure.

454
00:37:53,994 --> 00:37:57,007
Al-Khadr(الخضر) was instructed to build the wall.

455
00:37:58,740 --> 00:38:03,693
So the orphans would grow up and retrieve their treasure later.

456
00:38:04,946 --> 00:38:10,235
Because if the wall falls down; Al-Khadr(الخضر) left the wall alone, what would happen?

457
00:38:10,422 --> 00:38:14,435
It would fall down, and the treasure will be exposed.

458
00:38:14,949 --> 00:38:20,388
And these orphans are young, and they will not be able to defend their treasure.

459
00:38:20,628 --> 00:38:24,710
I mean, we know that the people of that town are not gonna leave that treasure alone.

460
00:38:24,823 --> 00:38:29,857
Those people who refuse to feed Al-Khadr(الخضر) and Musa(موسى); who refused to even give them some food;

461
00:38:30,130 --> 00:38:33,756
they're not gonna leave this treasure with two kids; they're gonna take it away from them.

462
00:38:34,162 --> 00:38:38,797
If these people were so miserable and stingy that they didn't even feed Musa(موسى) and Al-Khadr(الخضر);

463
00:38:39,257 --> 00:38:42,050
we wouldn't expect them to be honest with the two orphans.

464
00:38:42,337 --> 00:38:44,866
They're gonna steal that money; they're going to rip them off.

465
00:38:46,471 --> 00:38:50,537
Therefore Allah wanted Al-Khadr(الخضر) to build the wall again.

466
00:38:51,097 --> 00:38:58,036
So that, the orphans would grow up and when they're old and strong; they would be able to retrieve their treasure.

467
00:38:59,743 --> 00:39:01,130
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says;

468
00:39:01,570 --> 00:39:30,218
وَأَمَّا الْجِدَارُ فَكَانَ لِغُلَامَيْنِ يَتِيمَيْنِ فِي الْمَدِينَةِ وَكَانَ تَحْتَهُ كَنزٌ لَّهُمَا وَكَانَ أَبُوهُمَا صَالِحًا

469
00:39:31,325 --> 00:39:38,224
And as for the wall; it belong to two orphan boys in the town; and there was under it a treasure belonging to them;

470
00:39:38,477 --> 00:39:40,604
 and their father was a righteous man.

471
00:39:41,251 --> 00:39:42,197
Underline this.

472
00:39:42,691 --> 00:39:45,539
Why did Allah send the Al-Khadr(الخضر) to rebuild the wall?

473
00:39:46,025 --> 00:39:46,652
Why?

474
00:39:47,785 --> 00:39:51,814
Because the father of the two orphans was what?

475
00:39:52,288 --> 00:39:52,941
Righteous.

476
00:39:53,801 --> 00:39:59,570
Allah protected the orphans; Allah protected the children because the father was righteous.

477
00:40:00,477 --> 00:40:06,532
If you want Allah to protect your children; then protect them with your good deeds.

478
00:40:07,406 --> 00:40:09,212
Protect them with Al-Amal as-Salih(اَلْعَمَل اَلصَّالِحْ).

479
00:40:09,446 --> 00:40:15,095
Saeed ibn Musaiyyib(سعيد ابن مصيّب); Al-Taba'i Al-Kabir(التابعى الكبير); one of the major Taba'een(تابعين); he told his son;

480
00:40:15,381 --> 00:40:19,346
يابنئى انى لاستكثر من الاعمال الصالحة حتى يحفظك الله

481
00:40:19,708 --> 00:40:25,103
He said; Oh my son! I am doing so many good deeds, because I want the Allah to protect you with them.

482
00:40:26,730 --> 00:40:29,655
Our good deeds are protection for our children.

483
00:40:29,941 --> 00:40:35,001
If we want Allahسُبحانه وتعالى to take care of our children; let's take care of them by our good deeds.

484
00:40:35,728 --> 00:40:39,189
And Allahسُبحانه وتعالى will take care of them even if, you are not around.

485
00:40:39,576 --> 00:40:42,820
This man was dead; and Allahسُبحانه وتعالى took care of his orphans;

486
00:40:42,840 --> 00:40:44,540
Allah send Al-Khadr(الخضر) specifically,

487
00:40:44,800 --> 00:40:48,032
specifically send Al-Khadr(ال خضر) to go and fulfill that mission,

488
00:40:48,159 --> 00:40:48,865
why?

489
00:40:49,412 --> 00:40:52,684
To serve that man who died, because he was righteous.

490
00:40:53,644 --> 00:40:56,131
So Allahسُبحانه وتعالى will take care of your affairs; don't worry!

491
00:40:56,464 --> 00:41:01,490
Allah will take care of you; whether you're dead or alive; if you take care of the orders of Allah.

492
00:41:01,663 --> 00:41:02,903
احفظ الله يحفظك

493
00:41:03,550 --> 00:41:06,216
Take care of the commandments of Allah; what will happen?

494
00:41:06,443 --> 00:41:07,583
Allah will take care of you.

495
00:41:08,370 --> 00:41:37,131
وَكَانَ أَبُوهُمَا صَالِحًا فَأَرَادَ رَبُّكَ أَن يَبْلُغَا أَشُدَّهُمَا وَيَسْتَخْرِجَا كَنزَهُمَا رَحْمَةً مِّن رَّبِّكَ ۚ

496
00:41:37,991 --> 00:41:43,766
Their father was a righteous man and your Lord intended that they should attain their age of full strength,

497
00:41:43,806 --> 00:41:46,792
and take out their treasure as a mercy from your Lord.

498
00:41:47,059 --> 00:41:48,728
And then Al-Khadr(الخضر) is saying something important;

499
00:41:48,768 --> 00:41:50,448
وَمَا فَعَلْتُهُ عَنْ أَمْرِي ۚ

500
00:41:51,262 --> 00:41:54,597
And I did them not of my own accord.

501
00:41:54,791 --> 00:41:59,197
These things that you saw me do; Allah was one who's telling me to do them.

502
00:42:00,411 --> 00:42:01,523
This is knowledge from Allah.

503
00:42:02,096 --> 00:42:03,463
And that is how the believer should be.

504
00:42:03,503 --> 00:42:09,695
You never give credit to yourself, you give credit to whom the credit belongs to, and that is Allah.

505
00:42:10,915 --> 00:42:13,555
This is the story of Musa(موسى) and Al-Khadr(الخضر).

506
00:42:13,929 --> 00:42:15,641
Rasool Allah ﷺ says;

507
00:42:15,807 --> 00:42:21,494
يَرْحَمُ اللَّهُ مُوسَى ، لَوَكَانَ صَبَرَ يُقَصَّ عَلَيْنَا مِنْ أَمْرِهِمَا

508
00:42:21,694 --> 00:42:22,767
Rasool Allah ﷺ says;

509
00:42:22,834 --> 00:42:30,552
May Allah have mercy on Musa(موسى)! If he was patient; then we would have been told more about this amazing story.

510
00:42:30,805 --> 00:42:37,012
Rasool Allah ﷺ wants to know more about the details of the life of this learned, wise man; Al-Khadr(الخضر).

511
00:42:37,585 --> 00:42:47,701
We finish the story of Syedina Musaعليه السلام and we like to end his story by mentioning a few of his Fadha'il(فضائل); Manaqib(مناقب).

512
00:42:48,797 --> 00:42:52,630
These are not all of them; we'll just mention a few.

513
00:42:53,257 --> 00:42:57,650
Musaعليه السلام was the most frequently mentioned Nabi(نَبِي) in Qur'an.

514
00:42:59,423 --> 00:43:01,596
He was mentioned more than any other Nabi(نَبِي).

515
00:43:02,803 --> 00:43:08,066
And Allahسُبحانه وتعالى has praised Syedina Musa(سيدنا موسى) and said;

516
00:43:08,106 --> 00:43:09,719
وَكَانَ عِندَ اللَّهِ وَجِيهًا۝

517
00:43:11,106 --> 00:43:15,299
He was distinguished; he was noble; he was honoured.

518
00:43:16,666 --> 00:43:19,566
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى is the one who gave him that title.

519
00:43:21,079 --> 00:43:22,239
And Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says;

520
00:43:22,259 --> 00:43:28,114
وَاذْكُرْ فِي الْكِتَابِ مُوسَىٰ ۚ إِنَّهُ كَانَ مُخْلَصًا وَكَانَ رَسُولًا نَّبِيًّا۝

521
00:43:28,760 --> 00:43:37,956
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says; And mentioned in the book; Musa(موسى)! Verily he was chosen, and he was a messenger, and the prophet.

522
00:43:38,763 --> 00:43:39,713
He was chosen.

523
00:43:40,332 --> 00:43:40,989
مُخْلَصًا

524
00:43:41,029 --> 00:43:44,407
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى chose him from out of mankind.

525
00:43:44,713 --> 00:43:45,840
Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

526
00:43:45,933 --> 00:43:52,823
لا تفضلوني على موسى فإن الناس يصعقون يوم القيامة، فأكون أول من يفيق،

527
00:43:53,136 --> 00:44:04,424
واجدو موسی باتشا بقائمۃ العرش فلا ادری فصعق فافاق قبلی ام جوزی بصعق الطور رواہ البخاری و مسلم

528
00:44:04,737 --> 00:44:08,623
Rasool Allah ﷺ says; Don't prefer me over Musa(موسى).

529
00:44:08,823 --> 00:44:11,610
And we talked about what Rasool Allah ﷺ means by this.

530
00:44:11,876 --> 00:44:15,285
It is our belief and we know that, Muhammadﷺ is the best of mankind.

531
00:44:15,578 --> 00:44:20,835
But we know what Muhammadﷺ means of this; is his humbleness; صلی اللہ علیہ وسلم.

532
00:44:21,023 --> 00:44:22,530
Don't prefer me over Musa(موسى);

533
00:44:22,717 --> 00:44:29,786
Rasool Ullah does not want us to go to the non-believers and start saying;

534
00:44:29,806 --> 00:44:33,319
We have Muhammadﷺ you have Musa(موسى); Muhammadﷺ is better than Musa(موسى); No!

535
00:44:33,679 --> 00:44:42,032
Because Rasool Allah ﷺ does not want us to fight with the non-believers, and end up taking a stance against the Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء) of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى.

536
00:44:42,052 --> 00:44:45,079
Because Musa(موسى) is a Muslim and Eesa(عيسى) is a Muslim.

537
00:44:45,399 --> 00:44:47,918
Therefore, Rasool Allah ﷺ does not want us to get into that.

538
00:44:48,471 --> 00:44:48,705
He said;

539
00:44:48,725 --> 00:44:49,725
لا تفضلونا على موسى

540
00:44:49,771 --> 00:44:52,034
Don't say that, I am better than Musa(موسى).

541
00:44:52,501 --> 00:44:59,364
Because, Rasool Allah ﷺ says; On the Day of Judgment everybody will go through As-Sa'aq(صائق), that is the shock.

542
00:44:59,904 --> 00:45:04,365
 Everyone will go through that shock, and everyone will be unconscious and dead.

543
00:45:05,385 --> 00:45:06,748
And then Rasool Allah ﷺ says;

544
00:45:06,768 --> 00:45:18,873
And I will be the first one to rise up, but I will find out that Musa(موسى) is already grabbing the throne of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى.

545
00:45:19,866 --> 00:45:24,032
And I don't know whether, he was excluded from the shock

546
00:45:24,546 --> 00:45:30,718
or whether, he did not go through the shock because, he has already went through it when he asked to see Allah.

547
00:45:31,172 --> 00:45:34,037
You remember, when we talked about Musa(موسى) asking to see Allah;

548
00:45:34,177 --> 00:45:36,613
وَخَرَّصَعِقًا

549
00:45:36,773 --> 00:45:38,720
He went through a shock and he fell unconscious.

550
00:45:38,973 --> 00:45:43,285
So Muhammadﷺ said; Maybe Allah did not put him through the shock on the day of judgment

551
00:45:43,305 --> 00:45:45,772
because he has already been through a Shock in Duniyah(دُنِيَّا); that's enough.

552
00:45:46,152 --> 00:45:47,124
Once is enough.

553
00:45:47,338 --> 00:45:51,486
So, Musaعليه السلام will be excluded from that shock on the Day of Judgment.

554
00:45:52,552 --> 00:46:00,199
And Rasool Allah ﷺ once was distributing Al-Ghanaam(الغنام); the spoils of war; he was giving out.

555
00:46:00,659 --> 00:46:05,038
So one man came to Rasool Allah ﷺ and said;

556
00:46:05,798 --> 00:46:08,318
إن هذهِ لقسمةٌ ما يُرادُ بها وجهُ اللهِ

557
00:46:09,465 --> 00:46:16,033
He said; The way you're dividing this wealth, you're not doing it for the sake of Allah.

558
00:46:17,280 --> 00:46:22,304
A man comes to Rasool Allah ﷺ and tells him; You are not doing it, for the sake of Allah.

559
00:46:23,157 --> 00:46:33,480
Imagine this! You're speaking to the Messenger of Allah, whom Allahسُبحانه وتعالى to chose, and you accuse him of being unfair and unjust.

560
00:46:34,100 --> 00:46:35,627
Obviously, Rasool Ullah was upset.

561
00:46:36,333 --> 00:46:39,312
And the Sahabah(صحابه) said; We could see anger on his face.

562
00:46:40,592 --> 00:46:42,019
But then Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

563
00:46:42,039 --> 00:46:45,278
رَحِمَ اللَّهُ مُوسَى قدْ أُوذِيَ بأَكْثَرَ مِن هذا فَصَبَرَ

564
00:46:45,518 --> 00:46:49,864
May Allah have mercy on Musa(موسى)! He was harmed more than this, and he was patient.

565
00:46:50,470 --> 00:46:51,664
Musa(موسى) went through a lot.

566
00:46:51,764 --> 00:46:54,390
Allahسُبحانه وتعالى says, about Musa(موسى);

567
00:46:54,790 --> 00:46:58,748
يَا قَوْمِ لِمَ تُؤْذُونَنِي وَقَد تَّعْلَمُونَ أَنِّي رَسُولُ اللَّهِ إِلَيْكُمْ ۖ

568
00:46:58,782 --> 00:47:03,528
Oh my people! Why do you harm me, when you know that I'm the Messenger of Allah to you.

569
00:47:04,702 --> 00:47:06,406
So he went through a lot of harm.

570
00:47:07,446 --> 00:47:10,773
Nevertheless, he was patient, and Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

571
00:47:11,079 --> 00:47:14,327
May Allah have mercy on him! He went through more than this, and he was patient.

572
00:47:14,600 --> 00:47:18,237
Another one of the Fadha'il(فضائل) of Musaعليه السلام;

573
00:47:18,257 --> 00:47:22,780
Rasool Allah ﷺ mentioned one fadhilah(فضيله) for Musa(موسى) in Al-Asra(الاسراء) and one in Al-Mairaj(المعراج).

574
00:47:23,240 --> 00:47:27,986
When Rasool Allah ﷺ went to Al-Asra(الاسراء); Al-Asra(الاسراء) is a trip from Makkah(مكه) to Jerusalem,

575
00:47:28,219 --> 00:47:31,706
and Mairaj(معراج) is from Jerusalem to meet with Allahسُبحانه وتعالى.

576
00:47:31,824 --> 00:47:36,391
When Rasool Allah ﷺ was going in Al-Asra(الاسراء) from Makkah(مكه) to Jerusalem; Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

577
00:47:36,431 --> 00:47:41,712
I passed next to the grave of Musa(موسى), and I saw him praying in his grave.

578
00:47:42,739 --> 00:47:45,686
And then, when Rasool Allah ﷺ went in Al-Mairaj(المعراج);

579
00:47:45,980 --> 00:47:51,986
Rasool Allah ﷺ said; I met with Musa(موسى) in; As-Sama as-Sadisah(السماء السادسة); in the sixth heaven.

580
00:47:52,393 --> 00:47:56,347
Nobody was higher than Musa(موسى) except, Sayidina Ibrahimعليه السلام, in the seventh heaven.

581
00:47:56,787 --> 00:47:59,982
Musa(موسى) was the highest in the sixth heaven.

582
00:48:00,282 --> 00:48:05,615
That is one of the Faza'il(فضائل) of Syedina Musaعليه السلام.

583
00:48:06,928 --> 00:48:08,515
Rasool Allah ﷺ says;

584
00:48:09,142 --> 00:48:19,958
عُرِضَتْ عليَّ الأُممُ ، فرأيتُ النبيَّ ومَعهُ الرَّهْطُ ، والنبيَّ ومعهُ الرجُلَ والرَّجُلانِ ، والنبيَّ وليسَ مَعهُ أحَدٌ ،

585
00:48:20,638 --> 00:48:22,091
Rasool Allah ﷺ says;

586
00:48:23,018 --> 00:48:26,537
The umam(امم); the nations of the world were presented to me.

587
00:48:28,077 --> 00:48:32,270
I saw some prophets, they had a small group.

588
00:48:33,037 --> 00:48:37,226
Some of the prophets had a man or two, following them on the Day of Judgment.

589
00:48:37,259 --> 00:48:41,212
Imagine a Nabi(نَبِي) comes with one or two men with him, that's it.

590
00:48:41,419 --> 00:48:46,401
All of his life; he was making Da'wah(دعوة), and the result was one or two men, that's it.

591
00:48:47,014 --> 00:48:48,561
And then Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

592
00:48:49,214 --> 00:48:51,876
And I saw some of the Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء) and no one was with them.

593
00:48:52,129 --> 00:48:54,869
There were some Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء); they have no followers whatsoever.

594
00:48:55,249 --> 00:48:56,409
Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

595
00:48:56,676 --> 00:48:59,991
ثم عرض لِي سَوادٌ عظيمٌ ،

596
00:49:00,951 --> 00:49:03,258
And then I saw a huge nation.

597
00:49:04,258 --> 00:49:09,600
Rasool Allah ﷺ said; I desired; I wished that this would be my ummah(امة).

598
00:49:10,900 --> 00:49:12,087
أُمَّتي هذِه

599
00:49:12,127 --> 00:49:15,102
Rasool Ullah asked the two angels who are with him, Jibreel(جِبْرِيْل) and Mikail(ميكائيل).

600
00:49:15,456 --> 00:49:17,176
This is a dream, which Rasool Allah ﷺ was seeing.

601
00:49:17,402 --> 00:49:21,505
Jibreel(جِبْرِيْل) came and took his right hand; Mikail(ميكائل) his left hand and they took him in this trip.

602
00:49:21,772 --> 00:49:23,172
So, Rasool Ullah said; Is this my ummah(امة)?

603
00:49:23,212 --> 00:49:25,525
Rasool Ullah wanted this to be his ummah(امة); because this was huge.

604
00:49:25,845 --> 00:49:26,705
They said; No!

605
00:49:26,758 --> 00:49:28,523
هذِه اُمَّتِ مُوسى

606
00:49:28,543 --> 00:49:29,656
These are Bani Israel(بني أسرائيل).

607
00:49:29,896 --> 00:49:32,436
These are the ummah(امة) of Musa(موسى); Bani Israel(بني أسرائيل).

608
00:49:33,056 --> 00:49:34,320
But look to the right side!

609
00:49:34,953 --> 00:49:37,256
فَإِذَا بِسَوَادٌ عَظِيم يَمْلَأُ الأُفُقَ

610
00:49:37,673 --> 00:49:41,295
I look to the right side, and I saw a nation that is filling the horizon.

611
00:49:41,461 --> 00:49:43,648
And then, they told me; Look to the other side!

612
00:49:43,988 --> 00:49:48,264
So, I looked in the other side, and I saw a nation that is filling the horizon.

613
00:49:48,437 --> 00:49:50,691
They said this is your ummah(امة),

614
00:49:50,964 --> 00:50:01,293
and Allahسُبحانه وتعالى will include with them 70,000 of your ummah(امة) will enter into Jannah(جنة) without going through Hisaab(حساب);

615
00:50:01,727 --> 00:50:04,782
without going through the regular accounting of everyone else.

616
00:50:05,222 --> 00:50:13,141
70,000 of this ummah(امة) will enter into paradise without going through the accountability stage that everyone else has to go through.

617
00:50:14,301 --> 00:50:16,841
This is a Karamah(كرامه) of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى to this ummah(امة).

618
00:50:17,681 --> 00:50:23,593
But we also learned from the Hadith(حديث) that, the second largest nation is the nation of Bani Israel(بني أسرائيل); the children of Israel(اسرائيل).

619
00:50:24,486 --> 00:50:26,844
Another Hadith(حديث) narrated by Al-Imam Ahmad(الاِمَامْ اَحْمَدْ);

620
00:50:28,197 --> 00:50:32,613
Rasool Allah ﷺ when he went to Hajj(حَجْ); he passed through a valley,

621
00:50:33,366 --> 00:50:35,306
he asked; what is the name of this valley?

622
00:50:36,519 --> 00:50:37,773
قالو هذا وادي الازرق

623
00:50:38,006 --> 00:50:40,725
The name of this valley is the Azraq(ازرق) valley.

624
00:50:40,985 --> 00:50:42,038
Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

625
00:50:42,058 --> 00:50:52,464
كأني أنظر إلى موسى وهو هابطاً من الثنية، وله جؤار إلى الله عزوجل بالتلبية

626
00:50:52,870 --> 00:51:01,766
Rasool Allah ﷺ says; As if I can see Musa(موسى) coming down from this hill, making Hajj(حَجْ) to Allahسُبحانه وتعالى, and making Talbiyah(تلبيه).

627
00:51:03,133 --> 00:51:08,652
So, Musaعليه السلام made Hajj(حَجْ); He made Hajj(حَجْ) to the house of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى.

628
00:51:09,326 --> 00:51:10,732
Yunus Ibn matta(يونس ابن مطّه) made Hajj(حَجْ),

629
00:51:10,959 --> 00:51:15,695
and another Ahadith(احاديث); we have narrations of other Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء) making Hajj(حَجْ) like, Hud(هود) and Saleh(صالح).

630
00:51:15,935 --> 00:51:19,641
So the Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء) of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى; they made Hajj(حَجْ) to the house of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى,

631
00:51:19,768 --> 00:51:23,627
and Allah was making Muhammadﷺ see them, as if it was in front of his eyes.

632
00:51:23,820 --> 00:51:26,107
He saw Musa(موسى), when he was coming down that hill,

633
00:51:26,267 --> 00:51:32,403
and he saw Yunus ibn Matta(يونس ابن مطّه) coming down that hill, wearing wool clothes, over a red camel.

634
00:51:32,816 --> 00:51:36,999
These are some of the Fadha'il(فضائل) of Musaعليه السلام.

635
00:51:38,732 --> 00:51:42,892
صَلَّى الله عَلى سَيَّدِنَا محمد وَعَلى اَلِهِ وَ صَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ تسلیما کثیرا

